### Azka Maintenance Scheduling — End-to-End Test Requests
### Base: https://localhost:5001/api
### Flow: register -> login -> create assets/engineers -> work orders -> auto/manual assign -> reschedule -> status flow -> dashboard
###
### HOW TO RUN:
### 1) Run the backend:  dotnet run --project Azka.Web
### 2) Run requests below in order. After Login (request 4), copy the returned
###    "token" value into @adminToken below (replaces the placeholder).
### 3) Tip: create a second @engineerToken from Login with engineer@azka.dev (registered in request 2)
###    to test role restrictions.

@api = https://localhost:5001/api

### 1) REGISTER — Admin (do once; returns 409 if email already exists)
POST {{api}}/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Admin",
  "email": "admin@azka.dev",
  "password": "Admin123!",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### 2) REGISTER — Engineer (do once; for role-permission tests later)
POST {{api}}/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Engineer",
  "email": "engineer@azka.dev",
  "password": "Engineer123!",
  "role": "Engineer"
}

### 3) LOGIN — returns { token, ... }; copy token into @adminToken below
POST {{api}}/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@azka.dev",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### NEGATIVE TEST — wrong password should return 401 with an error message
POST {{api}}/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@azka.dev",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

@adminToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..movRGaXRq-FNvME9rCfHmd2mQe3kMDhiKP5yVYoBO-U
@engineerToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..ORYXrMHGRzRg_3yAg6T2ngjHi4I80XBSclIsVreuBEg
@id = 1

### 4) GET /Dashboard — health of the whole operation (any authenticated role)
GET {{api}}/Dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5) CREATE ASSETS — 2 smart meters at a customer address
POST {{api}}/Assets
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetNumber": "AST-1001",
  "assetType": 1,
  "address": "12 Rue de la Paix, Paris",
  "latitude": 48.8566,
  "longitude": 2.3522,
  "customerName": "Louvre SA",
  "installationDate": "2025-03-14T09:00:00Z"
}

### 6) CREATE ASSET — second one
POST {{api}}/Assets
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetNumber": "AST-1002",
  "assetType": 2,
  "address": "5 Av. des Champs, Lyon",
  "latitude": 45.7640,
  "longitude": 4.8357,
  "customerName": "Louvre SA",
  "installationDate": "2025-06-02T09:00:00Z"
}

### 7) LIST ASSETS — filter by customer
GET {{api}}/Assets?customerName=Louvre&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8) CREATE ENGINEER — North team, 8h capacity, working 08:00-16:00
POST {{api}}/Engineers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeNumber": "EMP-001",
  "fullName": "Marie Dupont",
  "email": "marie.dupont@azka.dev",
  "team": "North",
  "region": "Île-de-France",
  "skills": "Smart Meter, Gateway",
  "workingHours": "08:00-16:00",
  "dailyCapacityHours": 8
}

### 9) CREATE ENGINEER — South team
POST {{api}}/Engineers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeNumber": "EMP-002",
  "fullName": "Karim Benali",
  "email": "karim.benali@azka.dev",
  "team": "South",
  "region": "Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes",
  "skills": "Transformer, Gateway",
  "workingHours": "08:00-16:00",
  "dailyCapacityHours": 8
}

### 10) WORKLOAD — Marie, today (utilization % must reflect later assignments)
GET {{api}}/Engineers/1/workload?date=2026-08-03
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 11) AVAILABLE ENGINEERS — who can take a job in this window
GET {{api}}/Engineers/available?from=2026-08-03T09:00:00&to=2026-08-03T11:00:00
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12) CREATE WORK ORDER — Emergency, 2h, against AST-1001 (asset id 1)
POST {{api}}/WorkOrders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetId": 1,
  "maintenanceType": 3,
  "priority": 4,
  "estimatedHours": 2,
  "requestedDate": "2026-08-03T08:00:00Z",
  "dueDate": "2026-08-03T12:00:00Z",
  "notes": "Meter reporting no connectivity — customer escalation"
}

### 13) CREATE WORK ORDER — High, 3h, against AST-1002 (asset id 2)
POST {{api}}/WorkOrders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetId": 2,
  "maintenanceType": 1,
  "priority": 3,
  "estimatedHours": 3,
  "requestedDate": "2026-08-03T08:00:00Z",
  "dueDate": "2026-08-04T16:00:00Z",
  "notes": "Preventive check"
}

### 14) LIST WORK ORDERS — filter emergency
GET {{api}}/WorkOrders?priority=4&status=Open&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15) AUTO-ASSIGN — system picks the least-loaded capable engineer (order id 1)
POST {{api}}/Assignments/auto-assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workOrderId": 1,
  "scheduledStart": "2026-08-03T09:00:00",
  "scheduledEnd": "2026-08-03T11:00:00"
}

### 16) MANUAL ASSIGN — assign order 2 to engineer 2 (Karim)
POST {{api}}/Assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workOrderId": 2,
  "engineerId": 2,
  "scheduledStart": "2026-08-03T10:00:00",
  "scheduledEnd": "2026-08-03T13:00:00"
}

### 17) NEGATIVE TEST — overlapping window on same engineer must be rejected (409)
POST {{api}}/Assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workOrderId": 1,
  "engineerId": 2,
  "scheduledStart": "2026-08-03T10:30:00",
  "scheduledEnd": "2026-08-03T12:00:00"
}

### 18) LIST ASSIGNMENTS — status filter
GET {{api}}/Assignments?status=Assigned&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 19) RESCHEDULE — move assignment 1 earlier in the day
PUT {{api}}/Assignments/1/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newScheduledStart": "2026-08-03T08:30:00",
  "newScheduledEnd": "2026-08-03T10:30:00",
  "changeReason": "Customer opened earlier"
}

### 20) WORK ORDER -> IN PROGRESS (board drop: Assigned -> InProgress)
PATCH {{api}}/WorkOrders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 4
}

### 21) ASSIGNMENT -> COMPLETED
PATCH {{api}}/Assignments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 4
}

### 22) WORK ORDER -> COMPLETED (board drop: InProgress -> Completed)
PATCH {{api}}/WorkOrders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 5
}

### 23) WORK ORDER -> CANCELLED (negative path)
PATCH {{api}}/WorkOrders/2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": 6,
  "notes": "Customer cancelled request"
}

### 24) ROLE TEST — Engineer token trying to DELETE an engineer -> 403 Forbidden
DELETE {{api}}/Engineers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{engineerToken}}

### 25) DASHBOARD AFTER — verify completed/open/overdue counts moved
GET {{api}}/Dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
